"""Mutations of part 7b's actors (src/game/radio.*, document_place.*, mine.*, ts_explosion.*,
spawn_point.* and S_vector::NormalizedGame in src/ls3d/math.h) for ../mutfast.py with the actors
build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_objective.py --models DIR --build build_item.bat --check check_item.py

Each should make check_item.py fail (or the harness crash / hang). Left out as equivalent: the
actor messages' reliable flags (the harness's actor streams are made either way), the spawn point's
multiplayer uniform argument (CreateSoldier reads the state's there), its direction's w (never
read), the loading spawn's actor slot in multiplayer (the slot itself), the message's default stats
(overwritten in multiplayer, not passed in single player) and its state's profile index (the
message's), the spawn properties' empty-chunk test (Descend fails there too), the radio's material
self test (the frame's own id again), the documents' sector position (they lie at the frame's
origin), the mine's arm time stored before Arm (Arm stores it), NormalizedGame's unit test (a
float sum within 1e-8 of 1 is 1, scaled by 1 anyway), the creators' Destroy (memory only).

Results (2026-10-26): the first run of 667 caught 644; 2 survivors were equivalent (dropped,
above) and 21 needed new cases (literal TS states, a dirty volume before Arm, Defuse's reliable
flag, item type 0 and states 0 / 3 at the radio, the TS defaults and SetFrame / StartMission resets
from set values, the zone asked, the document place started / stopped again in another state,
waiting / stopped again with the volume in / out, the documents' place, Trigger from a running
time, a decal left before the client's, Setup from an armed mine). The rerun of those 21: all
caught; all 665 caught (23 of them by a crash)."""
